This repository is a scoped demonstration submitted to the Arm Create:
AI Optimization Challenge 2026 (Track 3: Mobile AI). It builds on top of
ExecuTorch (PyTorch Edge), which is separately licensed — see
https://github.com/pytorch/executorch for its license terms.

CI (`.github/workflows/build.yml`'s `qwen-export-pilot` job) exports and
distributes a quantized `.pte` build artifact derived from
Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct
(https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct), licensed under the
Apache License 2.0 per its model card (see the model card for full
attribution). This NOTICE credits that model as the source of the
distributed weights, per Section 4(d) of the Apache License 2.0 — the
same obligation that applies to TALON's own code, not just to the
vendored helper below.

`scripts/convert_qwen_checkpoint.py` includes a small helper function
(`get_mapped_key`) and a Qwen2.5 weight-key mapping adapted from
pytorch/torchtune (torchtune/models/convert_weights.py) and
pytorch/executorch (examples/models/qwen2_5/convert_weights.py), both
BSD-3-Clause licensed, Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.

